WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.490
Two babies, one zygote.

2
00:00:02.540 --> 00:00:06.000
Identical twins start
life with the same genome.

3
00:00:06.050 --> 00:00:10.630
Yet as the years pass, identical
twins become more different.

4
00:00:10.680 --> 00:00:14.320
Researchers study this by
comparing young and old pairs,

5
00:00:14.370 --> 00:00:17.260
and pairs who live together or apart.

6
00:00:17.310 --> 00:00:22.010
So if twins start with the same genes,
why do they become more different as they

7
00:00:22.060 --> 00:00:23.170
age?

8
00:00:23.220 --> 00:00:27.660
In this mission, you'll test that
question against data from twin pairs.

9
00:00:27.710 --> 00:00:31.060
Then you'll judge what a study
of people's blood cells can,

10
00:00:31.110 --> 00:00:33.120
and cannot, conclude.

11
00:00:33.170 --> 00:00:38.190
Your mission: explain why identical
twins grow more different as they age.
